meta:
  id: irb-post-study
  name: Post-Study Questionnaire
  version: 2.0.0
  description: |
    IRB 26-285 approved instrument (Survey Questionnaire 10.12.26 and
    SDG Knowledge Test 9.10.26). Wording is verbatim; do not edit without
    an IRB modification.
    K1-K3 repeat, then K4, E1-E8, A1-A2, F1-F2, AI0-AI2, B1-B4, T1-T3,
    O1-O5. Branching the importer can't express: AI1-AI2 only if AI0 is a
    Yes; B1-B4, P9 and T3 browser only; T2 only if T1 is a Yes.
    Browser payment needs K4, E1, E2, E3, E4, E5, E7 answered or declined.
  shortName: PostStudy
  tags: [irb-26-285, post]

questions:
  - id: K1
    text: "SDG 4 - Quality Education. Which statement best describes how libraries can advance Quality Education?"
    type: multiple_choice
    config:
      options:
        - "By limiting learning services to formally enrolled students"
        - "By expanding equitable access to education, information, digital technologies, and lifelong learning opportunities"
        - "By focusing only on preservation of historical materials"
        - "By providing emergency response services only"

  - id: K2
    text: "SDG 11 - Sustainable Cities and Communities. Which library activity is an example of strengthening sustainable and resilient communities?"
    type: multiple_choice
    config:
      options:
        - "Serving as a resilience hub that provides trusted information, internet connectivity, charging, safe space, and access to essential services during emergencies"
        - "Restricting community partnerships during emergencies"
        - "Reducing access to local cultural and historical information"
        - "Limiting civic participation to government agencies"

  - id: K3
    text: "SDG 13 - Climate Action. Which approach is described as a way libraries can advance Climate Action?"
    type: multiple_choice
    config:
      options:
        - "Avoiding environmental topics because they are outside the library role"
        - "Combining climate-literacy education with practical activities such as repair, reuse, makerspaces, and community partnerships"
        - "Providing climate information only to environmental professionals"
        - "Replacing community programs with building-efficiency projects alone"

  - id: K4
    text: "I learned something new from this experience."
    type: multiple_choice
    config:
      options:
        - "1 - Strongly disagree"
        - "2"
        - "3"
        - "4"
        - "5 - Strongly agree"
        - "Prefer not to answer"

  - id: E1
    text: "Overall, how engaging was this experience?"
    type: multiple_choice
    config:
      options:
        - "1 - Not at all engaging"
        - "2"
        - "3"
        - "4"
        - "5 - Extremely engaging"
        - "Prefer not to answer"

  - id: E2
    text: "Overall, how easy was it to navigate the environment?"
    type: multiple_choice
    config:
      options:
        - "1 - Very difficult"
        - "2"
        - "3"
        - "4"
        - "5 - Very easy"
        - "Prefer not to answer"

  - id: E3
    text: "How mentally demanding was the experience?"
    type: multiple_choice
    config:
      options:
        - "1 - Not at all demanding"
        - "2"
        - "3"
        - "4"
        - "5 - Extremely demanding"
        - "Prefer not to answer"

  - id: E4
    text: "How useful were the information presentations for understanding the SDGs?"
    type: multiple_choice
    config:
      options:
        - "1 - Not at all useful"
        - "2"
        - "3"
        - "4"
        - "5 - Extremely useful"
        - "Prefer not to answer"

  - id: E5
    text: "Overall, how satisfied were you with the experience?"
    type: multiple_choice
    config:
      options:
        - "1 - Very dissatisfied"
        - "2"
        - "3"
        - "4"
        - "5 - Very satisfied"
        - "Prefer not to answer"

  - id: E6
    text: "How likely would you be to use a similar learning experience again?"
    type: multiple_choice
    config:
      options:
        - "1 - Very unlikely"
        - "2"
        - "3"
        - "4"
        - "5 - Very likely"

  - id: E7
    text: "After this experience, how motivated are you to learn more about the SDGs?"
    type: multiple_choice
    config:
      options:
        - "1 - Not at all motivated"
        - "2"
        - "3"
        - "4"
        - "5 - Extremely motivated"
        - "Prefer not to answer"

  - id: E8
    text: "After this experience, how willing are you to take an action related to one or more of the SDGs?"
    type: multiple_choice
    config:
      options:
        - "1 - Not at all willing"
        - "2"
        - "3"
        - "4"
        - "5 - Extremely willing"

  - id: A1
    text: "Thinking back to when you first entered the SDG Discovery Hall, what type of information first caught your attention?"
    type: multiple_choice
    config:
      options:
        - "Written/text"
        - "Data visualization/interactive infographic"
        - "Narrative video/audio"
        - "Interactive activity/simulation"
        - "AI-enabled virtual docent"
        - "Something else"
        - "Do not remember"

  - id: A2
    text: "What is the first specific thing you remember noticing?"
    type: text

  - id: F1
    text: "Which type of information helped you learn the most?"
    type: multiple_choice
    config:
      options:
        - "Written/text"
        - "Data visualization/interactive infographic"
        - "Narrative video/audio"
        - "Interactive activity/simulation"
        - "AI docent"
        - "No single format"
        - "Other"

  - id: F2
    text: "Which type of information held your attention the most?"
    type: multiple_choice
    config:
      options:
        - "Written/text"
        - "Data visualization/interactive infographic"
        - "Narrative video/audio"
        - "Interactive activity/simulation"
        - "AI docent"
        - "No single format"
        - "Other"

  - id: AI0
    text: "Did you use the optional AI-enabled virtual docent during this study?"
    type: multiple_choice
    config:
      options:
        - "No"
        - "Yes, once"
        - "Yes, more than once"
        - "Not sure / do not remember"

  - id: AI1
    text: "How useful was the AI-enabled virtual docent?"
    type: multiple_choice
    config:
      options:
        - "1 - Not at all useful"
        - "2"
        - "3"
        - "4"
        - "5 - Extremely useful"

  - id: AI2
    text: "What, if anything, was useful or not useful about the AI docent?"
    type: text

  - id: B1
    text: "Which SDG zones did you visit during your exploration? Select all that apply."
    type: selection
    config:
      options:
        - "SDG 4 – Quality Education"
        - "SDG 11 – Sustainable Cities and Communities"
        - "SDG 13 – Climate Action"
        - "Not sure / do not remember"

  - id: B2
    text: "What was the first information element you selected or interacted with?"
    type: multiple_choice
    config:
      options:
        - "Written/text information"
        - "Data visualization/interactive infographic"
        - "Narrative video/audio"
        - "Interactive activity/simulation"
        - "AI-enabled virtual docent"
        - "Something else"
        - "Do not remember"

  - id: B3
    text: "Which types of objects or interactive elements did you use? Select all that apply."
    type: selection
    config:
      options:
        - "Text/information panels"
        - "Data visualizations/interactive infographics"
        - "Narrative video/audio"
        - "Interactive activities/simulations"
        - "AI-enabled virtual docent"
        - "Other"
        - "None / do not remember"

  - id: B4
    text: "Before beginning this post-study questionnaire, how would you describe the status of your exploration?"
    type: multiple_choice
    config:
      options:
        - "I considered my exploration complete"
        - "I chose to stop before I was finished"
        - "A technical or connection problem caused me to stop early"
        - "Another reason caused me to stop early"
        - "Not sure"

  - id: T1
    text: "Did you experience any technical difficulties?"
    type: multiple_choice
    config:
      options:
        - "No"
        - "Yes – minor, but I was able to continue"
        - "Yes – significant"

  - id: T2
    text: "If yes, please briefly describe the technical difficulty."
    type: text

  - id: T3
    text: "Browser only: During the study, did you experience connection-related problems such as slow loading, buffering, freezing, or disconnection?"
    type: multiple_choice
    config:
      options:
        - "No"
        - "Yes – minor, but I was able to continue"
        - "Yes – significant"
        - "Not sure whether the problem was my internet connection or the study itself"

  - id: O1
    text: "What stood out most to you during the experience?"
    type: text

  - id: O2
    text: "What, if anything, did you learn that was new to you?"
    type: text

  - id: O3
    text: "Was anything difficult, confusing, or frustrating?"
    type: text

  - id: O4
    text: "What would you change to improve the experience?"
    type: text

  - id: O5
    text: "Is there anything else you would like to share?"
    type: text
